  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\n\nThe core idea is to enhance the SDP-based approach by incorporating a novel smooth relaxation and adaptive parameter tuning. Unlike previous methods, this plan combines multiple optimization techniques: SDP for global structure, SLSQP for local refinement, and simulated annealing with smooth transformations. The goal is to escape local optima better by balancing exploration and exploitation through multi-stage optimization. \n\nKey metrics driving the search:\n- Use adaptive temperature scaling in SA\n- Employ a logarithmic barrier function for smoothness\n- Incorporate multiple scales: coarse grid SDP, fine grid refinement\n- Schedule hyperparameter adjustments based on progress\n\nThe main bottleneck in the current approach is sensitivity to initial conditions and slow convergence. This plan addresses it by:\na) Using SDP to define the global structure in coarse grid\nb) Smooth optimizing function to maintain feasibility\nc) Progressive refinement with annealing schedules\nd) Adaptive dimensionality (starting coarse and expanding)\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n\na) Representation:\n- Coarse grid: n_coarse = 400 grid points\n- Final grid: n_final = 600 (already provided parent)\n- Binary constraint: \u2211h_i = n/2 for all grids\n- h_i \u2208 [0,1] for all i\n\nb) Objective function:\nFor a candidate solution h of length L, compute:\nC5(h) = max_k \u222b_0^2 h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n(discrete approx via correlation)\n\nSmoothed objective for optimization:\nF(\u03b1,h) = max_k (corr_k) + \u03b1 \u00b7 (1/\u03c4) \u00b7 log(\u2211 exp(-\u03b1\u00b7E_k))\n\nwhere E_k is violation in constraints.\n\nc) Constraints:\n- Continuous smoothing with elasticity parameter \u03b1\n- Project to feasible space by minimizing (h_i - clip)^2 + 1/\u03b1 (MaxK - current_k)\n- Ensure: 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1 and \u2211h_i = n/2 \u00b1 \u03b5\n\nd) Variables:\n- Primary variables: h_i \u2208 \u211d for 1\u2264i\u2264n_coarse\n- SDP variables including Z_kk' for covariance and constraints\n\ne) Optimization algorithm:\n\nPhase 1: Coarse grid SDP-elastic (n=400)\n- Solve: minimize F(\u03b1_max) subject to h\u2208[0,1]^400\n- Use barrier parameter \u03b1_max, then reduce\n\nPhase 2: Fine grid interpolation (800 points)\n- Use projection mapping from coarse to fine grid\n\nPhase 3: Progressive refinement (600 points)\n- Start from coarse solution expanded to 600 points\n- Use SLSQP with adaptive alpha\n- Then simulated annealing with adaptive neighborhood\n\nf) Math operations:\n- Correlation computation for penalty\n- Log barrier for constraints\n- Smooth interpolation using Lagrange basis\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n\nDefine these helper functions:\ndef smooth_objective(h, alpha=1.5):\n    # core optimization function\n    \ndef project_feasible(h, target, alpha=1.5):\n    # encompassing binary projection with alpha\n\ndef solve_sdp(n):\n\nphase1_coarse = solve_sdp(n_coarse, seed=seed)\nh_interpolated = project_feasible(phase1_coarse, n_final, alpha=0.8)\nbest_score = compute_c5(h_interpolated)\n\n# Phase2: Progressive refinement\nfor iter in range(3):\n    if time_left < 10: break\n    h_i = np.append(h_interpolated, h_interpolated[-n_extra:])\n    best_i = hillclimb(h_i, alpha_max=1.2)\n    if compute_c5(best_i) < best_score: best_score, best_i = compute, update\n\n# Phase3: Final annealing\nsa_run(alpha_scheduled=True)\nreturn best_i, best_score, n_final\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations:\n\na) Default parameters:\n- Initial temperature: 0.02\n- Temperature decay: (0.9)^iteration\n- Alpha schedule: [0.8, 1.0, 1.2, 1.5]\n- Barrier reduction: multiplicative by 0.7 every 1000 iterations\n\nb) Variations to try when time allows:\n- Hybrid crossover between solutions\n- Multi-population annealing with seeding\n- Fractional grid expansion (n90, n_final)\n- adaptive grid increase (n=500, 700, 800)\n\nc) Condition triggers:\n- For each Annealing Neighborhood swap probability\n- If no improvement in N steps, reduce temperature\n- Dynamic dimension adjustments based on grid size\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness:\n\na) Time estimates:\n- SDP phase: ~400s for n=400 with multiple iterations\n- Refinement: ~500s (over several stages)\n- Allow 300s for SDP + 400s for refinement\n\nb) Idle time checks:\n- At start of SDP phase: check budget cutoff\n- Within SDP: periodic budget check\n- SA phase: temperature-based budget division\n\nc) Fallback mechanisms:\n- Keep best solution ever found\n- Safeguard against numerical overflow\n- Round coordinates when precision degrades\n\n6. Validation and return contract:\n\na) Penalties for infeasible solutions:\n- Positive penalty if \u2211h_i not within [-\u03b5, n/2+\u03b5]\n- Override score with 2.0 if infeasible\n\nb) Final criteria:\n- Evaluate C5(h) by compute_c5(h)\n- Enforce \u2211h_i = near n/2\n- h_i \u2208 [0,1] rounded to 3 decimals\n\nc) Requirements checking post-refinement:\n- \u03b5 = 1e-5 must satisfy: -\u03b5 \u2264 sum(h) - 300 \u2264 \u03b5\n- For any point: 0.9 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1.1 (considering rounding)\n- Compute difference: abs(computed_c5 - \u2016C5(parent)\u2016) \n\nd) Entitlement:\n- C5 should improve over parent's 0.380890\n- Target: C5 \u2264 parent's value with five decimal precision \n\nHandoff instructions: Implement with numpy and scipy optimization, use global state for best solution tracking. Maintain dimension information and allow explicit grid size adjustments via parameter. Use the provided `compute_c5` function as evaluation.",
